WEBVTT

00:12:58.124 --> 00:13:00.976
SM: You don't know?
Let me tell you something interesting.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.307
IM: You know what?
Stop laughing! It's not funny.

00:13:03.331 --> 00:13:06.530
Just because I don't know
there's no such thing as whole buttermilk.

00:13:06.554 --> 00:13:07.705
Sorry. What?

00:13:07.729 --> 00:13:11.067
SM: Here's the deal: in the old days,
when they used to make butter --

00:13:11.091 --> 00:13:12.477
You know how you make butter?

00:13:12.501 --> 00:13:13.794
IM: Churn.
SM: From cream.

00:13:13.818 --> 00:13:14.969
IM: Yeah, exactly.

00:13:14.993 --> 00:13:18.042
SM: So you take heavy,
high-fat milk, which is cream,

00:13:18.066 --> 00:13:22.606
and you churn it until it separates
into these curds and water.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:26.515
The liquid is actually -- if you've
ever overbeaten your whipped cream,

00:13:26.539 --> 00:13:28.181
it's actually buttermilk.

00:13:28.205 --> 00:13:29.976
That's what it was in the early days.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.976
And that's what people used
for baking and all sorts of things.